D. Proof-facing obstruction
  The broad-rank-6 hope is false, but the exception is finite:
    the six rescue owners form a connected overlap graph, and the
    maximal gate toggles are a mirror pair whose adjacent cover owners
    contain the whole rescue subset.  The only extra max-delta owner is
    173, so the gluing problem is a seven-owner local clause, not a
    global scalar obstruction.
  Menger cut route: treat the two max-delta survivor gates as terminals
    in the branch-coloured blocker graph and prove any full saturation
    would cut off the low-rank HYP-3450/HYP-3451 escape component.
  Schwarz-Christoffel route: the gate endpoints are labelled prevertices;
    the mirror pair supplies the boundary-order involution, while cover
    delta (3,4)/(4,3) is the accessory-parameter payload.
  Bring/BDH/SPEC route: any monodromy or averaging sidecar is legal only
    after this finite seven-owner clause is retained.

